# Fix My Campus – Prototype Wireframes

**Status:** Initial Design Concepts / Subject to Team Review

## Overview

These wireframes demonstrate how the Fix My Campus application could look and function.

The main aim is to create a simple interface that allows students to report issues quickly while providing staff with an organised way to manage them.

These are early design concepts and may change as development progresses.

## Proposed Screens

| Screen | Purpose | Main Elements | Proposed Epic |
|---|---|---|---|
| Home Page | Introduce the application and direct users to its main functions. | Report Issue button, Track Issue button, navigation. | User Interface |
| Report Issue | Allow students to submit campus problems. | Issue title, category, location, description, optional photo. | Issue Reporting |
| Submission Confirmation | Confirm that a report has been submitted successfully. | Confirmation message and reference number. | Issue Reporting |
| Track Issue | Allow users to check the progress of a report. | Reference number lookup and status information. | Issue Tracking |
| Staff Dashboard | Allow maintenance and IT staff to manage submitted reports. | Issue list, filters, categories and status controls. | Staff Management |
| Mobile View | Make the application accessible on smaller screens. | Responsive navigation and simplified layout. | User Interface |

## Design Considerations

- Keep the layout simple and easy to navigate.
- Allow anonymous issue reporting.
- Make the reporting form quick to complete.
- Use clear issue categories and status labels.
- Ensure staff can quickly identify and manage reports.
- Make the interface usable on desktop and mobile devices.

## Next Steps

The team will review these initial designs, decide which screens to include in the first release and refine them based on the agreed user stories.

Each final wireframe must be linked to its actual Jira story key and epic, with its creator identified.

**Note:** These wireframes are prototype design suggestions, not completed or approved application screens.
